WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.237
-When Donald Trump lost
by 7 million votes in 2020,

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.939
many assumed
the Republican Party

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.208
would quickly jettison him,
but the opposite has happened.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.843
The GOP is refusing
to move on from Trump.

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:13.479
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:17.249 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:19.018
When Trump lost,
there was a hope

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.953
we could all move on
and talk about something else.

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:22.322
In a perfect world,

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:25.124
right now I'd be hosting a show
called "Major Crimes,"

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.492
which would be a round-up

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:29.028
of who Joe Biden's German
shepherd had attacked that week.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.263
I'd host in a trench coat

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.365
like Robert Stack in
"Unsolved Mysteries."

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.599
"While it's always been known

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:35.501
for back-stabbing
and dirty dealings,

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:39.372
this week, Washington, D.C.,
went to the dogs."

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.407
That would have been the show.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:42.842
But, of course,
it did not work out like that.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.845
In fact, as we pointed out
many times before the election,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.080
that was never gonna happen.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.281
Trump didn't
come out of nowhere,

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.683
and the toxic political culture
he exposed

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.519
wasn't simply gonna vanish.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.922
Even after he left office,
the conditions that created him

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.991
and the destruction he left
behind would inevitably remain.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:01.060
We always knew that
would be the case.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.330
We just didn't know Republicans
themselves would be so eager

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.066
to cling to the abject failure
that was the Trump era.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.934
They're like a bunch
of burnt-out uncles

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.303
reliving their high school
football glory days.

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:13.006
But they weren't
the star quarterback.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.606
They were the backup punter

00:01:14.606 --> 00:01:17.911
and they lost the state
championship by 7 million votes.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:21.347
Now, it's worth noting that's
not how they've always felt,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.283
especially during Trump's
second impeachment.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.085
Trump incited a violent mob
of insurrectionists,

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.686
a mob that ransacked
the Capitol,

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:28.921
attacked police officers,

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:30.757
and threatened to
kill the Vice President

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.526
in order to disrupt the lawful
counting of electoral votes.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.829
And when it came time to
hold him accountable for that,

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.931
Republicans told us
to just let it go

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:40.933
since Trump was on his way out
anyway.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:42.068
-I'm ready to move on.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.470
I'm ready to end
the impeachment trial

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.407
because I think it's
blatantly unconstitutional.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.443
I'm ready to get on with trying
to solve the nation's problems.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.944
-I think the country
needs to move forward.

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:54.113
We've got a lot of issues
that we need to be working on.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.647
-They hate Donald J. Trump,

00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:59.986
and they're engaging in an act
that I think is petty.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.988
I think it is retribution.
I think it is vindictive.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:04.490
And I think it's
a waste of time.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.361
And so, to coin a phrase,
I think it's time to move on.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.696
-I'm sure Ted Cruz has heard
that phrase a lot in his life.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:12.231
"Ted, this relationship
isn't working.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:13.232
It's time to move on."

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.300
"Ted, the beard,
it's not a thing.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.402
It's time to move on."

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.270
"Ted, Carly is not coming back.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:19.605
It's time to move on."

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:24.143
-The next President of the
United States -- Ted Cruz.

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.478
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.478 --> 00:02:28.080
-Remember that,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.515
when Ted Cruz chose
a running mate

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.618
and then she, I guess,
fell down an open manhole

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:34.186
and disappeared forever?

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:36.656
She probably staged that
just to get away from Ted Cruz.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.590
"Don't worry, Carly,
I'll come and get you."

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.727
"That's okay. I actually
like it down here with
the sewer people."

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.729
"This is a sewer?

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.131
I thought it was the F train.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:48.134
Oh, Rudy! Ya dope!"

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.436
These guys backed
nearly everything Trump did

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.737
for four years.

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:54.007
Then the second he incited
a violent insurrection,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.674
they told us all to move on.

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:58.511
Like, Marco Rubio had an
especially cynical explanation

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.413
for why he thought the media
and the left were so obsessed

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:02.848
with impeaching Trump

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:05.051
for the crime of trying
to violently overthrow democracy

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.819
instead of just letting him
off the hook.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.921
-This is not the right use
of Congress' time.

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:10.156
It's vindictive.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.191
This is all about
the left's demand for revenge.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:14.327
And I'm gonna be frank,
some of the people out there

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.162
in the political entertainment
business,

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:18.264
this is about ratings
and about clicks

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.066
because this is another drama
story that adds to the show.

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:23.002
-The only reason Donald Trump
was good for ratings

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.470
is he was bad for
everything else.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.372
He was good for ratings
in the same way

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.474
that hurricanes are great
for The Weather Channel.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.610
"Honey, it's channel 4-1-7."

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.213
His presidency was
a once-in-a-century catastrophe

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.649
filled with corruption, chaos,
misery, and suffering.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.818
Of course people
wanted to stay informed.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.519
That's like saying
a zombie apocalypse

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.488
would be good
for ham radio sales.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:45.924
"Hello? Hello, we are
seven survivors in Denver.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:48.727
Where are you? Brains?

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:51.163
Where is that? Wisconsin?

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:54.500
Load up the van. We're going to
Brains, Wisconsin."

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.268
But that was then.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.237
Same Republicans who told us
to move on from Trump

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.072
after he incited
a violent insurrection

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.875
are now clinging to Trump
like doomsday preppers

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.144
clinging to a plastic bag
filled with gas.

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:07.579
And side note, guys. Let's, you
know, just stop hoarding gas.

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:08.847
This isn't "Mad Max."

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:10.817
He's President Joe,
not Immortan Joe.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.484
What's next, Sean Hannity
hosting a show

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:14.119
as The Doof Warrior?

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:15.988
"Did I say it right?"

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.890
We'll find out
in next week's corrections.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.425
NBC is putting us on prime time

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.695 line:0%
and rebranding it
as "Chicago Corrections."

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:26.532
"Bad news, boss,
you got another flub."

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.735
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.840
Anyway, the point is Republicans
have made it very clear

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.809
that Donald Trump
is the leader of their party now

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.611
and for the foreseeable future,

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.547
and they're refusing to move on
from the disastrous Trump years.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.916
-We are a pro-America
populist party

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.918
rooted in
conservative principle

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.719
with Donald Trump as our leader.

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:50.789
-To try to erase Donald Trump
from the Republican Party

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:52.491
is insane.

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.027
And the people
who try to erase him

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.994
are going to wind up
getting erased.

00:04:55.994 --> 00:04:58.364
It's impossible for this party
to move forward

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:01.200
without President Trump
being its leader.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.136
-They look at Donald J. Trump,

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:07.607
and they look at the millions
and millions of people inspired,

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.776
who went to battle, fighting
alongside President Trump,

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:12.845
and they're terrified.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:15.914
And they want him to go away.

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:17.550
Let me tell you this right now.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.619
Donald J. Trump
ain't going anywhere.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.487
-First of all,
there's nothing more grading

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.389
than Ted Cruz trying
to fire up a crowd.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.658
He might actually have
negative charisma.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:28.627
He sounds the way
hot dog water smells.

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:30.396
He's the guy casinos bring in

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.564
when there's a hot roller
at the craps table.

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:33.933
"Come on, lucky seven.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.135
Oh, no. Snake eyes.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:38.937
Too bad. So sad."

00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:40.639
I think Cruz is right that
Trump isn't going anywhere

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:42.307
but only in the literal sense,

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:44.077
that he physically
does not go anywhere.

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:45.711
He never leaves Mar-a-Lago.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:46.913
The most exercise he gets

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.781
is kicking his ball
back onto the fairway

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:49.982
and wandering from room to room,

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.484
interrupting various
private events

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.486
like a guy on a business trip
at a Radisson

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:54.987
looking for
the right conference room.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.421
"Is this
the voter fraud meeting?"

00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:57.923
"No, it's a wedding reception."

00:05:57.923 --> 00:06:00.159
"Would you like me to say
a few words about voter fraud?"

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.394
Trump's like an improviser
who has an audience plant

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:03.696
yell out suggestions.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.597
"Can I get a location?"
"Wedding."

00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:07.800
"Can I get a topic?"
"Voter fraud."

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.036
"We take you there now."

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.638
In fact, Republicans are
so deeply attached to Trump,

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.574
despite how horrendous he was
for the country,

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.542
they can't seem to stop
talking about him,

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.210
as Fox News pointed out
during an interview

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.645
with Mitch McConnell this week.

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:24.149
-Since April 24th, fundraising
e-mails from Republicans

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:26.719
have mentioned
the former President 97 times,

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.854
an average of more than
five times a day.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.256
You're saying the focus
is not on the past,

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:33.492
but you're using
the former President's name,

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:36.929
and Republicans are,
to raise money for 2022.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.731
-Five times a day.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.766
Republicans talk about Trump
more than I talk about

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:42.502
my Vince Vaughn impression.

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:44.269
"Geez, man, give it a rest."

00:06:44.269 --> 00:06:46.038
Ooh, I did a switcheroo.

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:48.141
In fact, one of the those
Republicans is Marco Rubio,

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:50.109
the same guy who claimed
it was the left

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:52.144
who is obsessed with Trump
for ratings and clicks.

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:54.347
Rubio sent out a fundraising
e-mail this week

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:57.149
bragging about the fact that
he was one of the first people

00:06:57.149 --> 00:07:00.019
mentioned by name
on Trump's new blog.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.188
Rubio wrote
in a fundraising e-mail,

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:05.424
"I was lucky enough to be
one of his first posts."

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:07.626
It should be noted that
this is the same blog

00:07:07.626 --> 00:07:09.127
that the former President used

00:07:09.127 --> 00:07:12.865
to call Kentucky Derby winner
Medina Spirit a junky.

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.600
And I know there are some
out there

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.068
who think we should ignore

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:19.372
when a former President
calls a horse a junky.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:22.808
Well, I just want to say,
no can do.

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:25.211
I don't have the strength
to ignore it

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:28.213
when a grown man hears a horse
failed a drug test

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:30.583
and then calls the horse
a junky.

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:33.319
Not now, not ever.

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:36.488
Wish I could.
But I can't.

00:07:36.488 --> 00:07:38.658
Also, can it get more pathetic
than Rubio saying

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:40.860
"I was lucky enough to be
one of his first posts"?

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.894
Republicans talk about Trump
the way teens at a concert

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:44.230
talk about One Direction.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.732
"Jenna, oh, my God,
he looked at me.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.701
Harry looked at me. He made
direct eye contact with me.

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.670
Jenna, did you see that?

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:55.041
Jenna, did you see him
look right at my direct eyes?

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:57.943
Jenna, are you listening?
Harry Styles looked at me,

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.345
Jenna,
and now we're gonna get married.

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:01.614
And, Jenna, you're not coming,
Jenna.

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:04.383
You're not coming
because you didn't believe me.

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.318
You didn't believe me, Jenna."

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:08.287
"Oh, wait. Oh, hold on.

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.222
No, he's looking at you, Jenna."

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:12.157
Republicans are obsessed
with Trump

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:13.859
because they have
no central ideology

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:15.795
other than their hostility
toward democracy.

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:17.729
The big lie that
the election was stolen

00:08:17.729 --> 00:08:19.064
is their only core belief.

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:20.966
And I'm guessing a lot of them
don't even believe it.

00:08:20.966 --> 00:08:22.568
They just know that Trump does.

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:25.805
When I was in college and a girl
wanted to read my tarot cards,

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:27.906
I definitely acted like
I was interested

00:08:27.906 --> 00:08:29.975
in what the page of cups meant.

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:32.111
But Republicans know they can
weaponize Trump's big lie

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:33.479
to make it harder
for people to vote

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:35.681
and, thus, easier for the GOP
to win elections.

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.617
That's why their number-one
legislative priority

00:08:37.617 --> 00:08:40.352
is codifying Trump's big lie
through voter suppression laws

00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:42.220
so they can rig the game
in their own favor.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:45.057
They've calculated that
they don't need to appeal

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:46.592
to a majority of Americans

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:49.061
the way a healthy democracy
normally works

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:52.198
if they can just exploit
antidemocratic methods

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:54.033
like gerrymandering
and electoral college

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:56.334
to stay in power,
which is why they've decided

00:08:56.334 --> 00:08:58.537
to stay so closely tied
to Trump.

00:08:58.537 --> 00:09:00.739
In a way, you can see
how the incentives work.

00:09:00.739 --> 00:09:02.141
It's like, in a normal world,

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:03.976
the Jets have to get better
in order to win games,

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:06.445
but if they can pass legislation
only making it legal

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:09.114
for opposing teams to score on
Tuesdays from 9:00 A.M. to noon,

00:09:09.114 --> 00:09:10.783
they'd be in way better shape.

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:12.751
"Touchdown -- Chiefs. And that's
not good for the Jets.

00:09:12.751 --> 00:09:15.220
Wait. Hold on.
The ref is running over,

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:18.390
and Patrick Mahomes' signature
is not an exact match.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.259
They're taking the points
off the board."

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:22.194
The point is,
Republicans have calculated

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:23.728
they don't need democracy,

00:09:23.728 --> 00:09:26.532
so they can stick by
a deeply unpopular ex-President

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.900
who never once
cracked 50% job approval

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.169
and never won the popular vote.

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:32.571
In fact, they're so openly
hostile to democracy,

00:09:32.571 --> 00:09:34.373
they're actually
excusing the mob

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:36.375
that seized the Capitol
on January 6th,

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:39.645
as we saw yesterday when
GOP Congressman Andrew Clyde

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:43.082
said the insurrection looked
more like a group of tourists.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.583
-There was no insurrection.

00:09:44.583 --> 00:09:46.652
And to call it an insurrection,
in my opinion,

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.620
is a bold-faced lie.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.290
Watching the TV footage of those
who entered the Capitol

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.359
and walked through Statuary Hall

00:09:53.359 --> 00:09:55.227
showed people
in an orderly fashion

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:56.962
staying between
the stanchions and ropes

00:09:56.962 --> 00:09:58.631
taking videos and pictures.

00:09:58.631 --> 00:10:00.465
